the trace name in the hover labels for all traces. -1 shows the whole
name regardless of length. 0-3 shows the first 0-3 characters, and an
integer >3 will show the whole name if it is less than that many
characters, but if it is longer, will truncate to `namelength - 3`
characters and add an ellipsis. Integer in the interval [-1, Inf], or
a vector of these.}

\item{showarrow}{Sets whether or not to show the hover label
arrow/triangle pointing to the data point. Logical.}

\item{color}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_hoverlabel_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_textfont()}}: Color: a CSS color string or R
  color name, or a vector of these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_legendgrouptitle_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: Color: a CSS
  color string or R color name.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_line()}}: Sets the line color. Color: a
  CSS color string or R color name.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker()}}: Sets the marker color. It
  accepts either a specific color or an array of numbers that are mapped
  to the colorscale relative to the max and min values of the array or
  relative to `marker.cmin` and `marker.cmax` if set. Color: a CSS color
  string or R color name, or a number mapped to a color by
  \code{scattersmith.marker.colorscale}, or a vector of these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker_gradient()}}: Sets the final
  color of the gradient fill: the center color for radial, the right for
  horizontal, or the bottom for vertical. Color: a CSS color string or R
  color name, or a vector of these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker_line()}}: Sets the marker.line
  color. It accepts either a specific color or an array of numbers that
  are mapped to the colorscale relative to the max and min values of the
  array or relative to `marker.line.cmin` and `marker.line.cmax` if set.
  Color: a CSS color string or R color name, or a number mapped to a
  color by \code{scattersmith.marker.line.colorscale}, or a vector of
  these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_selected_marker()}}: Sets the marker
  color of selected points. Color: a CSS color string or R color name.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_selected_textfont()}}: Sets the text
  font color of selected points. Color: a CSS color string or R color
  name.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_unselected_marker()}}: Sets the marker
  color of unselected points, applied only when a selection exists.
  Color: a CSS color string or R color name.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_unselected_textfont()}}: Sets the text
  font color of unselected points, applied only when a selection exists.
  Color: a CSS color string or R color name.}

\item{family}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_hoverlabel_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_textfont()}}: HTML font family - the typeface
  that will be applied by the web browser. The web browser can only
  apply a font if it is available on the system where it runs. Provide
  multiple font families, separated by commas, to indicate the order in
  which to apply fonts if they aren't available. String, or a vector of
  these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_legendgrouptitle_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: HTML font family
  - the typeface that will be applied by the web browser. The web
  browser can only apply a font if it is available on the system where
  it runs. Provide multiple font families, separated by commas, to
  indicate the order in which to apply fonts if they aren't available.
  String.}

\item{lineposition}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_hoverlabel_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_textfont()}}: Sets the kind of decoration
  line(s) with text, such as an "under", "over" or "through" as well as
  combinations e.g. "under+over", etc. Any combination of
  \code{"under"}, \code{"over"}, \code{"through"} joined with
  \code{"+"}, or one of \code{"none"}, or a vector of these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_legendgrouptitle_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: Sets the kind of
  decoration line(s) with text, such as an "under", "over" or "through"
  as well as combinations e.g. "under+over", etc. Any combination of
  \code{"under"}, \code{"over"}, \code{"through"} joined with
  \code{"+"}, or one of \code{"none"}.}

\item{shadow}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_hoverlabel_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_textfont()}}: Sets the shape and color of the
  shadow behind text. "auto" places minimal shadow and applies contrast
  text font color. See
  https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/text-shadow for
  additional options. String, or a vector of these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_legendgrouptitle_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: Sets the shape
  and color of the shadow behind text. "auto" places minimal shadow and
  applies contrast text font color. See
  https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/text-shadow for
  additional options. String.}

\item{size}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_hoverlabel_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_textfont()}}: Number in the interval [1, Inf],
  or a vector of these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_legendgrouptitle_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: Number in the
  interval [1, Inf].

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker()}}: Sets the marker size (in
  px). Number in the interval [0, Inf], or a vector of these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_selected_marker()}}: Sets the marker
  size of selected points. Number in the interval [0, Inf].

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_unselected_marker()}}: Sets the marker
  size of unselected points, applied only when a selection exists.
  Number in the interval [0, Inf].}

\item{style}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_hoverlabel_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_textfont()}}: Sets whether a font should be
  styled with a normal or italic face from its family. One of
  \code{"normal"}, \code{"italic"}, or a vector of these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_legendgrouptitle_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: Sets whether a
  font should be styled with a normal or italic face from its family.
  One of \code{"normal"}, \code{"italic"}.}

\item{textcase}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_hoverlabel_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_textfont()}}: Sets capitalization of text. It
  can be used to make text appear in all-uppercase or all-lowercase, or
  with each word capitalized. One of \code{"normal"}, \code{"word
  caps"}, \code{"upper"}, \code{"lower"}, or a vector of these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_legendgrouptitle_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: Sets
  capitalization of text. It can be used to make text appear in
  all-uppercase or all-lowercase, or with each word capitalized. One of
  \code{"normal"}, \code{"word caps"}, \code{"upper"}, \code{"lower"}.}

\item{variant}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_hoverlabel_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_textfont()}}: Sets the variant of the font. One
  of \code{"normal"}, \code{"small-caps"}, \code{"all-small-caps"},
  \code{"all-petite-caps"}, \code{"petite-caps"}, \code{"unicase"}, or a
