  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_legendgrouptitle_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: Sets the variant
  of the font. One of \code{"normal"}, \code{"small-caps"},
  \code{"all-small-caps"}, \code{"all-petite-caps"},
  \code{"petite-caps"}, \code{"unicase"}.}

\item{weight}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_hoverlabel_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_textfont()}}: Sets the weight (or boldness) of
  the font. Integer in the interval [1, 1000], or a vector of these.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_legendgrouptitle_font()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
  \code{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: Sets the weight
  (or boldness) of the font. Integer in the interval [1, 1000].}

\item{backoff}{Sets the line back off from the end point of the nth line
segment (in px). This option is useful e.g. to avoid overlap with
arrowhead markers. With "auto" the lines would trim before markers if
`marker.angleref` is set to "previous". Number in the interval [0,
Inf], or a vector of these.}

\item{dash}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_line()}}: Sets the dash style
  of lines. Set to a dash type string ("solid", "dot", "dash",
  "longdash", "dashdot", or "longdashdot") or a dash length list in px
  (eg "5px,10px,2px,2px"). One of \code{"solid"}, \code{"dot"},
  \code{"dash"}, \code{"longdash"}, \code{"dashdot"},
  \code{"longdashdot"}, or a string matching
  \code{"^\\\\d+(\\\\.\\\\d+)?(px|\%)?((,|\\\\s)\\\\s*\\\\d+(\\\\.\\\\d+)?(px|\%)?)*$"}.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker_line()}}: Sets the dash style of
  lines. Set to a dash type string ("solid", "dot", "dash", "longdash",
  "dashdot", or "longdashdot") or a dash length list in px (eg
  "5px,10px,2px,2px"). One of \code{"solid"}, \code{"dot"},
  \code{"dash"}, \code{"longdash"}, \code{"dashdot"},
  \code{"longdashdot"}, or a string matching
  \code{"^\\\\d+(\\\\.\\\\d+)?(px|\%)?((,|\\\\s)\\\\s*\\\\d+(\\\\.\\\\d+)?(px|\%)?)*$"},
  or a vector of these.}

\item{shape}{Determines the line shape. With "spline" the lines are
drawn using spline interpolation. The other available values
correspond to step-wise line shapes. One of \code{"linear"},
\code{"spline"}.}

\item{smoothing}{Has an effect only if `shape` is set to "spline" Sets
the amount of smoothing. 0 corresponds to no smoothing (equivalent to
a "linear" shape). Number in the interval [0, 1.3].}

\item{width}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_line()}}: Sets the line width
  (in px). Number in the interval [0, Inf].

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker_line()}}: Sets the width (in px)
  of the lines bounding the marker points. Number in the interval [0,
  Inf], or a vector of these.}

\item{angle}{Sets the marker angle in respect to `angleref`. Angle in
degrees, or a vector of these.}

\item{angleref}{Sets the reference for marker angle. With "previous",
angle 0 points along the line from the previous point to this one.
With "up", angle 0 points toward the top of the screen. One of
\code{"previous"}, \code{"up"}.}

\item{autocolorscale}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker()}}:
  Determines whether the colorscale is a default palette
  (`autocolorscale: true`) or the palette determined by
  `marker.colorscale`. Has an effect only if in `marker.color` is set to
  a numerical array. In case `colorscale` is unspecified or
  `autocolorscale` is true, the default palette will be chosen according
  to whether numbers in the `color` array are all positive, all negative
  or mixed. Logical.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker_line()}}: Determines whether the
  colorscale is a default palette (`autocolorscale: true`) or the
  palette determined by `marker.line.colorscale`. Has an effect only if
  in `marker.line.color` is set to a numerical array. In case
  `colorscale` is unspecified or `autocolorscale` is true, the default
  palette will be chosen according to whether numbers in the `color`
  array are all positive, all negative or mixed. Logical.}

\item{cauto}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker()}}: Determines
  whether or not the color domain is computed with respect to the input
  data (here in `marker.color`) or the bounds set in `marker.cmin` and
  `marker.cmax` Has an effect only if in `marker.color` is set to a
  numerical array. Defaults to `false` when `marker.cmin` and
  `marker.cmax` are set by the user. Logical.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker_line()}}: Determines whether or
  not the color domain is computed with respect to the input data (here
  in `marker.line.color`) or the bounds set in `marker.line.cmin` and
  `marker.line.cmax` Has an effect only if in `marker.line.color` is set
  to a numerical array. Defaults to `false` when `marker.line.cmin` and
  `marker.line.cmax` are set by the user. Logical.}

\item{cmax}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker()}}: Sets the upper
  bound of the color domain. Has an effect only if in `marker.color` is
  set to a numerical array. Value should have the same units as in
  `marker.color` and if set, `marker.cmin` must be set as well. Number.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker_line()}}: Sets the upper bound of
  the color domain. Has an effect only if in `marker.line.color` is set
  to a numerical array. Value should have the same units as in
  `marker.line.color` and if set, `marker.line.cmin` must be set as
  well. Number.}

\item{cmid}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker()}}: Sets the mid-point
  of the color domain by scaling `marker.cmin` and/or `marker.cmax` to
  be equidistant to this point. Has an effect only if in `marker.color`
  is set to a numerical array. Value should have the same units as in
  `marker.color`. Has no effect when `marker.cauto` is `false`. Number.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker_line()}}: Sets the mid-point of
  the color domain by scaling `marker.line.cmin` and/or
  `marker.line.cmax` to be equidistant to this point. Has an effect only
  if in `marker.line.color` is set to a numerical array. Value should
  have the same units as in `marker.line.color`. Has no effect when
  `marker.line.cauto` is `false`. Number.}

\item{cmin}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker()}}: Sets the lower
  bound of the color domain. Has an effect only if in `marker.color` is
  set to a numerical array. Value should have the same units as in
  `marker.color` and if set, `marker.cmax` must be set as well. Number.

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker_line()}}: Sets the lower bound of
  the color domain. Has an effect only if in `marker.line.color` is set
  to a numerical array. Value should have the same units as in
  `marker.line.color` and if set, `marker.line.cmax` must be set as
  well. Number.}

\item{coloraxis}{Sets a reference to a shared color axis. References to
these shared color axes are "coloraxis", "coloraxis2", "coloraxis3",
etc. Settings for these shared color axes are set in the layout, under
`layout.coloraxis`, `layout.coloraxis2`, etc. Note that multiple color
scales can be linked to the same color axis. Subplot id:
\code{"coloraxis"}, \code{"coloraxis2"}, \code{"coloraxis3"}, ....}

\item{colorbar}{Named list or
\code{\link{go_scattersmith_marker_colorbar}()} object.}

\item{colorscale}{\strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker()}}: Sets the
  colorscale. Has an effect only if in `marker.color` is set to a
  numerical array. The colorscale must be an array containing arrays
  mapping a normalized value to an rgb, rgba, hex, hsl, hsla, hwb, or
  named color string. At minimum, a mapping for the lowest (0) and
  highest (1) values are required. For example, `[[0, 'rgb(0,0,255)'],
  [1, 'rgb(255,0,0)']]`. To control the bounds of the colorscale in
  color space, use `marker.cmin` and `marker.cmax`. Alternatively,
  `colorscale` may be a palette name string of the following list:
  Blackbody,Bluered,Blues,Cividis,Earth,Electric,Greens,Greys,Hot,Jet,Picnic,Portland,Rainbow,RdBu,Reds,Viridis,YlGnBu,YlOrRd.
  Colorscale: a vector of colors, a two-column data.frame of (value,
  color), or the name of a sequential, diverging or cyclical scale in
  \code{\link{px_colors}()} (append \code{"_r"} to reverse).

  \strong{\code{go_scattersmith_marker_line()}}: Sets the colorscale.
  Has an effect only if in `marker.line.color` is set to a numerical
  array. The colorscale must be an array containing arrays mapping a
  normalized value to an rgb, rgba, hex, hsl, hsla, hwb, or named color
  string. At minimum, a mapping for the lowest (0) and highest (1)
  values are required. For example, `[[0, 'rgb(0,0,255)'], [1,
  'rgb(255,0,0)']]`. To control the bounds of the colorscale in color
  space, use `marker.line.cmin` and `marker.line.cmax`. Alternatively,
  `colorscale` may be a palette name string of the following list:
  Blackbody,Bluered,Blues,Cividis,Earth,Electric,Greens,Greys,Hot,Jet,Picnic,Portland,Rainbow,RdBu,Reds,Viridis,YlGnBu,YlOrRd.
  Colorscale: a vector of colors, a two-column data.frame of (value,
  color), or the name of a sequential, diverging or cyclical scale in
  \code{\link{px_colors}()} (append \code{"_r"} to reverse).}

